; DOMAIN: stable-infinity-category [CLOSED, derived 2026-07-24]
; Claim: A stable infinity-category is a pointed infinity-category C with a zero object in which every fiber sequence is a cofiber sequence and vice versa; equivalently the loop/suspension adjunction (Omega, Sigma) is an equivalence. Consequences: C is enriched in spectra, its homotopy category Ho(C) is triangulated (distinguished triangles = fiber/cofiber sequences, shift = suspension autoequivalence), and finite limits agree with finite colimits (biproducts/pushout=pullback squares). Stabilization Sp(C)=lim(... -> C_* -Omega-> C_* -Omega-> ...) is the universal stable infinity-category receiving a functor from C; Sp = Sp(Spaces) is the initial presentable stable infinity-category (spectra), with smash as symmetric-monoidal unit S. A t-structure is a pair of full subcategories (C_{>=0}, C_{<=0}) with truncation functors; the heart C^heart is abelian and recovers classical homological data (e.g. D(A) has heart A). Exact functors preserve finite (co)limits = fiber/cofiber sequences.
; Bridge: genesis_infinity_category (stable = extra exactness condition on an infinity-category; localizations/limits are the infinity-categorical ones) + genesis_stable_homotopy (Sp is the universal stabilization; spectra, smash product, suspension are its objects/structure) + genesis_derived_category (Ho of a stable infinity-cat is triangulated; D(A) is the homotopy category of a stable infinity-cat with t-structure heart A — the derived category is the 1-categorical shadow).
(= (stable-infinity-category $C) (and (pointed $C) (fiber-equals-cofiber $C)))
(= (fiber-equals-cofiber $C) (equivalence (loop-functor $C) (inverse (suspension-functor $C))))
(= (stabilization $C) (limit-tower $C loop-functor))
(= (spectra) (stabilization Spaces))
(= (t-structure $C) (pair (connective $C) (coconnective $C)))
(= (heart $C) (intersection (connective $C) (coconnective $C)))
(= (exact-functor $F) (preserves $F fiber-cofiber-sequences))